          "path": "tests/progress_token_identity_proof.mjs",
          "sha256": "42b979c08be2212aca214b930314b0aeae192c43f3bf881535202e2ec977437c"
        }
      ],
      "decision": "The authenticated full-file source transition and current token census identify these exact public InjectionToken constructor roles: LEGACY_ANIMATION_MODE constructed with literal LEGACY_ANIMATION_MODE at line 22; LEGACY_ANIMATIONS_TEST_OVERRIDE constructed with literal LEGACY_ANIMATIONS_TEST_OVERRIDE at line 34. The newly owned LEGACY_ANIMATION_MODE and existing LEGACY_ANIMATIONS_TEST_OVERRIDE are distinct from each other, MATERIAL_ANIMATIONS, the public progress default token and same-description lookalikes in the genuine current Injector protocol. Actual ambient policy and component lifecycle remain separate. The source inventory reconciles all 25 imports and all 27 current constructions against the prior named roles: one historical local progress-default construction was replaced with the public peer alias, while the distinct legacy animation-mode construction was added; equal counts are not identity proof. The untouched 16.2.14 tagged source and SRI-verified package show that original legacy progress exported and injected the same nonlegacy progress token; current 22.1.7 public Injector and extracted defaults-branch protocols support that alias. Native component factories/rendering, ambient motion, consumer artifacts, advertised runtime floors, security and G11 remain separate."
    }
